p('For every finite d, C_d decreases in either price and in d. Its maximum-norm price Lipschitz constant is at most B*mu, and -B*mu&lt;partial C_d/partial d&lt;0. The deployed nominal upper allowance U_hat, its fixed point q_star and its contraction bound rho are unchanged. Therefore the same top-price orbit a_0=A, a_(j+1)=U_hat(a_j) dominates every permitted price pair phase by phase and attains the smallest actual surplus.')
p('r_j(d)=C_d(a_j,a_j) still descends to C_star(d)=C_d(q_star,q_star). Thus G_K(d)=sum_(j=0..K-1)r_j(d)/K is the tight worst long-run average, and every finite average from the first real cap is at least G_K(d). Guard-only has the same all-start long-run floor C_star(d); one immediate startup cap additionally protects every finite activation average at that floor. Without this startup cap, do not assert that finite-prefix guarantee from arbitrary old prices.')
p('For unknown fixed d in [0,d_bar], the worst endpoint is d_bar. A signed lower bound G_K(d_bar)&gt;=F consequently protects the entire declared interval. This is not a probability statement or an empirically calibrated confidence interval. The nominal action correspondence is external and fixed; a guard recomputed from uncertain actual parameters is a different problem.')
