p('For F&gt;0 and G_K(0)&gt;F, strict decrease gives one crossing d_crit. The stationary cap/guard crossing has the separate formula log(S_hat(z,z))-log(exp(F/(B*mu))-1), with z=A or q_star. A simple sufficient radius is the positive nominal reserve divided by B*mu. Finite-period roots use signed interval endpoints; all positive crossing widths are at most 1e-20. The 64-term saved price orbit and uniform geometric price tail remain enclosed rather than replaced by invented limit rewards.','Small')
